# Expectation record for 10_declarations_and_types/002_typedef_and_scope.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 002_typedef_and_scope
area               = 10_declarations_and_types
description        = Typedef declaration, block scope, and shadowing in the tag, member and label namespaces
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Shadowing is confined to the tag, member and label namespaces, because ordinary-identifier
shadowing is rejected by the mandated -Wshadow -Werror gate.  Every object is assigned
before it is read, every arithmetic result stays inside the range of int, and no jump
bypasses an initialisation that is later read.  No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
tag_scope=8 26
member_ns=11 100
typedef_scope=7 11
sibling_blocks=1 2
label_ns=1
END
